# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machine that maintains this repo, so by default
# git rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout. For most of the site that is harmless.
#
# For thriveproject it is NOT. That page is a byte-exact build product: _src/build.js
# regenerates index.html from a template plus base64 assets, and the build is verified
# with a byte-for-byte compare. If git normalises line endings on checkout, a fresh clone
# on Windows produces a template with CRLF, the build emits a 7.6MB file with different
# bytes, `build.js --check` fails for no real reason, and the deployed page churns.
#
# -text disables all EOL conversion for these paths. Do not remove it.
thriveproject/index.html          -text
thriveproject/_src/template.html  -text
thriveproject/_src/build.js       -text
thriveproject/_src/config.json    -text

# embedded media: never touched by EOL rules, marked explicitly so diffs stay quiet
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
